[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186100869,
      "id": "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140",
      "title": "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f88a7380-4078-56ee-89c4-1a1286f3c84c",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$J=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -1 \\\\ -7 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$K=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$L=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 & 9 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -9 & -8\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $J,K,$ and $L?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $J$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, $K$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, and $L$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $J$ and $2$ rows in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $J$ equals the number of rows in $L,$ the matrices $J$ and $L$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{J}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{L}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $4$ columns in $L$ and $3$ rows in $K.$ Since the number of columns in $L$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $K$, the matrices $L$ and $K$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{L}_{2\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{K}_{3\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $K$ and $4$ rows in $J.$ Since the number of columns in $K$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $J$, the matrices $K$ and $J$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{K}_{3\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{J}_{4\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nThe product $JL$ is well defined. The products $LK$ and $KJ$ are undefined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "f6d50ca3-bf0b-5049-8633-b86e7b0350fe",
          ":answer-field/key": "The product $JL$ is well defined.",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "945a941e-9d7b-57fe-8e99-26a21b846356",
