    "question": {
      ":question/id": "204ee27f-04b2-5a2d-b00d-31e4cf7ce8ad",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 9 & -9\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 9 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $A,B,$ and $C?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $A$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, and $C$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{B}_{2\\times 4}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $4$ columns in $A$ and $4$ rows in $C.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $C,$ the matrices $A$ and $C$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{C}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $B$ and $2$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{A}_{2\\times 4}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nThe product $AC$ is well defined. The products $AB$ and $BA$ are undefined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0260281d-0823-58cb-a28b-59e08fe3be6f",
