    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "41e1ed09-730b-5c42-9c53-194863ae424d",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$L=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 7 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -3 & -8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$M=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$N=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $L,M,$ and $N?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $L$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, $M$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, and $N$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $N$ and $3$ rows in $M.$ Since the number of columns in $N$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $M,$ the matrices $N$ and $M$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{N}_{2\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{M}_{3\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $M$ and $2$ rows in $N.$ Since the number of columns in $M$ equals the number of rows in $N,$ the matrices $M$ and $N$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{M}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{N}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $N$ and $2$ rows in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $N$ equals the number of rows in $L,$ the matrices $N$ and $L$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{N}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{L}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe products $MN$ and $NL$ are well defined. The product $NM$ is undefined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "b6dab3ae-e558-5296-b9e4-8e2bc02e86a8",
          ":answer-field/key": "The product $NM$ is well defined.",
