  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186100869,
      "id": "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140",
      "title": "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b3caf718-efe5-5e64-b06a-96f77f9770ee",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$D=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$E=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 1 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$F=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 4 & 5 & 9 \\\\ -7 & -8 & 2 & -6 \\\\ -2 & -7 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $D,E,$ and $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $D$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, $E$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, and $F$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $F$ and $2$ rows in $E.$ Since the number of columns in $F$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $E,$ the matrices $F$ and $E$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{F}_{4\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{E}_{2\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $D$ and $2$ rows in $E.$ Since the number of columns in $D$ equals the number of rows in $E,$ the matrices $D$ and $E$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{D}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{E}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $F$ and $2$ rows in $D.$ Since the number of columns in $F$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $D,$ the matrices $F$ and $D$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{F}_{4\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{D}_{2\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nThe product $DE$ is well defined. The products $FE$ and $FD$ are undefined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "52dffc85-39e0-57ac-9bf6-4c2341380637",
          ":answer-field/key": "The product $FE$ is well defined.",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "7eeac787-4066-5033-93f1-4de062ab55e9",
