    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f6f82f6b-8077-5106-9ad2-bcab7c2dd0d2",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$J=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$K=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -1 & 7 \\\\ -7 & -5 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$L=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 7 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $J,K,$ and $L?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $J$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $K$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, and $L$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $K$ and $4$ rows in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $K$ equals the number of rows in $L,$ the matrices $K$ and $L$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{K}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{L}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $L$ and $3$ rows in $J.$ Since the number of columns in $L$ equals the number of rows in $J$, the matrices $L$ and $J$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{L}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{J}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $J$ and $2$ rows in $K.$ Since the number of columns in $J$ equals the number of rows in $K$, the matrices $J$ and $K$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{J}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{K}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe products $KL$ and $LJ$ and $JK$ are well defined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "6a9e0759-27f0-5847-9ad1-3dd017e9c7d0",
          ":answer-field/key": "The product $KL$ is well defined.",
