  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186100869,
      "id": "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140",
      "title": "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "488162c0-86d0-5d8e-8ce9-364bd6a873bb",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$X=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & -9 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$Y=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -7 \\\\ -6 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$Z=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -5 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $X,Y,$ and $Z?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $X$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix, $Y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, and $Z$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $Z$ and $3$ rows in $X.$ Since the number of columns in $Z$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $X,$ the matrices $Z$ and $X$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{Z}_{3\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{X}_{3\\times 4}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $4$ columns in $X$ and $3$ rows in $Z.$ Since the number of columns in $X$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $Z,$ the matrices $X$ and $Z$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{X}_{3\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{Z}_{3\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $Z$ and $2$ rows in $Y.$ Since the number of columns in $Z$ equals the number of rows in $Y,$ the matrices $Z$ and $Y$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{Z}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{Y}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe product $ZY$ is well defined. The products $ZX$ and $XZ$ are undefined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "72853c04-a921-523f-9f41-0ff3516e774c",
          ":answer-field/key": "The product $ZX$ is well defined.",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "d154237c-fc8c-5f7d-a033-c766636da28a",
