    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "56081c9a-cc45-5ef5-aa65-0a945e3a3838",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$D=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & -8 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 6 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -1 & -8 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$E=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -6 \\\\ 8 & -9\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$F=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -9\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $D,E,$ and $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $D$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix, $E$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, and $F$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $D$ and $4$ rows in $F.$ Since the number of columns in $D$ equals the number of rows in $F,$ the matrices $D$ and $F$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{D}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{F}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $E$ and $3$ rows in $D.$ Since the number of columns in $E$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $D,$ the matrices $E$ and $D$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{E}_{2\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{D}_{3\\times 4}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $F$ and $2$ rows in $E.$ Since the number of columns in $F$ equals the number of rows in $E,$ the matrices $F$ and $E$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{F}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{E}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe products $DF$ and $FE$ are well defined. The product $ED$ is undefined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "328b5448-7318-54c2-9771-aacc56283ea0",
          ":answer-field/key": "The product $DF$ is well defined.",
